{"type":"assistant.message","data":{"messageId":"a33811d8-8540-465a-a816-440a2d74021a","content":"The problem was a stacking context. `.canvas-rce-shell` has `backdrop-filter`, which makes it its own stacking context, so the panel's `z-index: 60` only counts inside the shell. The shell's own `z-index: 10` was being ignored because it had no `position` set. That left the whole shell, panel included, below the `.controls` tooltips at 30/40.\n\nThe fix is in [app.css](packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/app.css#L64-L69): I gave the shell `position: relative` and raised its `z-index` to 50. That's above the tooltips (30/40) and below the fullscreen preview (100), so the order is now option → panel → tooltip for both hover and non-hover.\n\nI regenerated the scaffold snapshot, but I haven't checked the change in the browser yet.","toolRequests":[],"reasoningText":"I could quickly check the browser, but the localhost:5173 dev page is likely just the docs tool and may not reflect this properly, so I'll keep it brief.\n\n"},"id":"142802a6-9b26-47b6-a433-a267d155a4a8","timestamp":"2026-09-25T17:40:51.469Z","parentId":"b5fc5554-c643-435a-89e6-afe09089892f"}
